       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is 5 times the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision (800 mg four times daily). The over-the-counter limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and CNS and metabolic toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), the maximum prescribed dose, usually for inflammatory conditions\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you want to confirm the dose or indication first, check with your resident or attending or with pharmacy."
